      "description": "CSUCI Jobs -\n\t\n\tCSU Channel Islands Skip to Content Accessible Browsing Information Menu Search Campus Go Academics Admissions & Costs Visit Campus Student Life About Give myCI Library Directory Maps Events Back to top CSUCI Jobs Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Job Type Open Date Close Date Lecturer AY - Public and Global Affairs Temporary September 04, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Political Science and Public Administration Program Executive Assistant to the VPBFA & Coordinator for Strategic Initiatives Regular September 02, 2026 September 16, 2026 Provides high-level confidential administrative support to the Interim Vice President for Business & Financial Affairs/CFO (VPBFA) and Executive Director of Budget, Resource Planning and Analysis by providing executive coordination of the Divisions' strategic planning and multi-channel communications, operationalization of special initiatives and projects, and provides leadership in maintaining an atmosphere of collegiality and professionalism in the Vice President's office, ensuring administrative functions and processes operate smoothly. Exercises considerable independent judgment, discretion, and initiative in supporting executive leadership, managing confidential matters, and fostering collaboration. Serves as liaison among University leadership, faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Supports the VPBFA's strategic administrative initiatives by independently coordinating special projects, advancing divisional priorities, improving organizational effectiveness, and coordinating complex initiatives that span multiple departments and stakeholders. Director, Facilities Operations Regular September 02, 2026 September 23, 2026 Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Facilities Services & Public Works, the Director of Facilities Operations provides leadership, management, and operational oversight for the maintenance, repair, and operation of the University’s buildings, grounds, infrastructure, utility systems, and related physical assets.\n\nThe Director is responsible for developing and maintaining a comprehensive, coordinated, and service-oriented facilities operations program that includes routine, preventive, predictive, corrective, and emergency maintenance. The position ensures that campus facilities and infrastructure are maintained in a safe, reliable, functional, compliant, and fiscally responsible manner in support of the University’s academic mission, student success, business continuity, and long-term stewardship of public resources. As a member of the Facilities Services & Public Works leadership team, the Director provides strategic and operational guidance to the Associate Vice President. LatinX Cultural Center Coordinator Regular September 02, 2026 September 16, 2026 Serves as a member of the Cultural Centers team and is responsible for the development, coordination, and ongoing operation of the LatinX Cultural Center. The coordinator designs, implements, and assesses culturally responsive programs and services that support the success, retention, and sense of belonging of Latinx and historically underserved student populations at California State University Channel Islands. The coordinator also contributes to campus-wide education and engagement by fostering greater awareness and understanding of diverse cultures, identities, and lived experiences, promoting an inclusive environment that benefits the entire university community. \n\nThis position plays a critical role in advancing CSUCI’s commitment as a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) by fostering identity development, strengthening student engagement, and building cross-campus and community partnerships. The coordinator contributes to an integrated cultural center model, ensuring cohesive, identify-affirming support systems aligned with institutional priorities related to student success, equity, and social mobility. Assistant or Associate Professor – Business (Operations) Regular September 02, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | MVS School of Business and Economics Academic Program Analyst Regular September 01, 2026 Provides a variety of complex administrative and analytical duties in support of the assigned academic programs. ESRM Technician Regular August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 Support laboratory, geospatial, field-based, and experiential instruction for the ESRM program. Ensure safe and effective operation of ESRM instructional laboratories and equipment and field-based instruction. Learning Designer Regular August 27, 2026 Designs, implements, supports, and evaluates faculty development efforts focused on digital learning ( online, blended, and technology-enhanced learning experiences) at CSU Channel Islands. Supports the growth, development, and optimization of online and blended courses and programs. Works with the Director of Digital Learning to cultivate a vision of innovation for digital learning experiences. Lecturer AY - Music Temporary August 20, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Dance, Music, and Theatre Lecturer AY - Theatre and Performance Studies Temporary August 06, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Dance, Music, and Theatre Lecturer AY - Psychology Temporary August 05, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Psychology Program Chief of Police Regular August 03, 2026 The Chief of Police provides executive leadership and overall direction for the CSU Channel Islands University Police Department and is responsible for protecting life and property, promoting a safe and secure campus environment, preventing and responding to crime and disorder, and supporting the safety and well-being of students, employees, visitors, and the broader campus community. The Chief is responsible for enforcing applicable federal, state, and local laws, as well as California State University and CSUCI rules, regulations, and policies.\nThe position oversees law enforcement operations, crime prevention, investigations, police communications and the 9-1-1 Public Safety Answering Point, records and CJIS compliance, property and evidence functions, Clery Act support, emergency management, business continuity, transportation and parking services, and related public safety programs. The Chief also serves as a visible campus leader responsible for professional standards, accreditation, community trust, equity and inclusion, and effective partnerships across CSUCI and with external public safety agencies. Lecturer AY - Spanish Temporary July 21, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Global Languages and Cultures Program Lecturer AY - Studio Art: Ceramics Temporary June 06, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Art Program Lecturer AY - Computer Science & Engineering Temporary May 29, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Computer Science & Engineering Lecturer AY - US History Temporary May 07, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | History Program Lecturer AY - Doctorate Educational Leadership Temporary February 19, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | School of Education Lecturer AY - Anthropology Temporary February 17, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Anthropology Program Police Officer Regular January 08, 2026 Provides service and protection to the university community, students, faculty, and staff from accidents, criminal activity, and other illegal behaviors that disrupt or negatively impact the educational environment. Serves as a sworn peace officer of the state and as such performs general and specialized law enforcement duties, conducts investigations, enforces laws and traffic regulations, makes arrests, conducts crime prevention and community policing program activities, and provides information and assistance to the general public. CI- Lecturer Faculty- Environmental Science and Resource Management (ESRM) Temporary November 10, 2025 Faculty Affairs Use Only\n------\nDivision of Academic Affairs | Environmental Science & Resource Management More Jobs 12 Current Opportunities Position Job Type Open Date Close Date Lecturer AY - Public and Global Affairs Temporary September 04, 2026 Division of Academic Affairs | Political Science and Public Administration Program Executive Assistant to the VPBFA & Coordinator for Strategic Initiatives Regular September 02, 2026 September 16, 2026 Provides high-level confidential administrative support to the Interim Vice President for Business & Financial Affairs/CFO (VPBFA) and Executive Director of Budget, Resource Planning and Analysis by providing executive coordination of the Divisions' strategic planning and multi-channel communications, operationalization of special initiatives and projects, and provides leadership in maintaining an atmosphere of collegiality and professionalism in the Vice President's office, ensuring administrative functions and processes operate smoothly. Exercises considerable independent judgment, discretion, and initiative in supporting executive leadership, managing confidential matters, and fostering collaboration. Serves as liaison among University leadership, faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Supports the VPBFA's strategic administrative initiatives by independently coordinating special projects, advancing divisional priorities, improving organizational effectiveness, and coordinating complex initiatives that span multiple departments and stakeholders. Director, Facilities Operations Regular September 02, 2026 September 23, 2026 Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Facilities Services & Public Works, the Director of Facilities Operations provides leadership, management, and operational oversight for the maintenance, repair, and operation of the University’s buildings, grounds, infrastructure, utility systems, and related physical 